# When an oust happens (zero-vtes rules-qa batches 45, 88, 101 and 118): a Methuselah whose pool
# reaches 0 or below is ousted then, as part of the effect that ran it out, with nothing played in
# between (45.1, ANK 20220210): here, as the command that ran it out ends. A cost paid
# out of turn may be a last pool: its payer is ousted at once, mid-action (101.3, 88.2). Pools run
# out by separate triggers go one after the other, in the order the acting Methuselah sets (118.1,
# 118.2, LSJ 20090208-2): each oust pays its predator before the next pool is judged.
# Seating A B C D E: A's prey is B, B's C, C's D, D's E, E's A.
seed 5
seat A alice
seat B bob
seat C carol
seat D dave
seat E erin
crypt A "Vera Nightfall" *12
library A "Iron Ward" *40
crypt B "Tomas Grey" *12
library B "Quick Feed" *40
crypt C "Ilse Várga" *12
library C "Gate Hound" *40
crypt D "Vera Nightfall" *12
library D "Iron Ward" *40
crypt E "Tomas Grey" *12
library E "Quick Feed" *40
start

A> transfer +4 A:uncontrolled:1
A> move A:uncontrolled:1 ready
A> transfer +4 A:uncontrolled:1
A> move A:uncontrolled:1 ready
B> pool -28
C> pool -29
expect pool A 22
expect pool B 2

# 45.1: Alice bleeds Bob for 4 with 2 pool left. He is ousted as the bleed resolves, nothing played
# in between; an ousted Methuselah keeps no pool. Alice gains the VP and 6 pool.
A> next
A> next
A> bleed A:ready:1
B> pass
A> resolve success 4
expect ousted B true
expect pool B 0
expect vp A 1
expect pool A 28

# 101.3, 88.2: Alice's other vampire bleeds Carol, her prey now. Carol pays her last pool as a cost
# out of turn (a card canceling the bleed, say): she is ousted at once, before the bleed resolves,
# and the bleed goes no further. Alice gains the VP and 6 pool.
A> bleed A:ready:2
expect action bleed A blocks
C> pool -1
expect ousted C true
expect action none
expect vp A 2
expect pool A 34

# 118.1, 118.2: one effect burns 4 pool from Dave (3 left) and from Erin, his prey (2 left), by
# separate triggers (minions lost together). Alice, acting, sets the order: Erin's first. Erin is
# ousted and Dave gains 6 pool before his own burn is judged, which then leaves him in the game.
# (A pool is changed down to 0 at most: Erin burns the 2 she has.)
D> pool -27
E> pool -28
E> pool -2
expect ousted E true
expect vp D 1
expect pool D 9
D> pool -4
expect pool D 5
expect ousted D false
